{"h": {"measure": "A", "k": 100}, "sp": "fc", "rep": 210, "hyps": [{"edit_param": "learning_rate_init", "edit_dir": "up", "cond_param": "learning_rate_init", "cond_band": "high", "direction": "lower", "why": "Raising an already-large learning rate pushes Adam into divergence, causing large accuracy collapses (#9, #12, #18)."}, {"edit_param": "learning_rate_init", "edit_dir": "up", "cond_param": "learning_rate_init", "cond_band": "low", "direction": "higher", "why": "At tiny learning rates the network is undertrained after 243 epochs, so a step up gives clear gains (#1-4, #19)."}, {"edit_param": "learning_rate_init", "edit_dir": "down", "cond_param": "learning_rate_init", "cond_band": "high", "direction": "higher", "why": "Stepping down from a diverging learning rate recovers training and yields large improvements (#89-96)."}, {"edit_param": "learning_rate_init", "edit_dir": "down", "cond_param": "learning_rate_init", "cond_band": "low", "direction": "lower", "why": "Lowering an already-small learning rate further slows convergence and hurts accuracy, unlike the large gains seen at high rates."}, {"edit_param": "alpha", "edit_dir": "up", "cond_param": "alpha", "cond_band": "high", "direction": "lower", "why": "Increasing an already-strong L2 penalty causes underfitting, with consistent drops (#73, #74, #83, #84)."}, {"edit_param": "alpha", "edit_dir": "up", "cond_param": "alpha", "cond_band": "low", "direction": "higher", "why": "At negligible alpha, a one-step increase barely changes the model, so the effect is near zero rather than negative (#69, #70, #82)."}, {"edit_param": "depth", "edit_dir": "up", "cond_param": "learning_rate_init", "cond_band": "high", "direction": "lower", "why": "Deeper networks are less stable at high learning rates, so adding a layer there causes big drops (#57, #58, #63, #64)."}, {"edit_param": "batch_size", "edit_dir": "up", "cond_param": "learning_rate_init", "cond_band": "high", "direction": "higher", "why": "Larger batches reduce grad